Effect: the outpost gives no fuel; the bunker route could not do its work; Atria, which starts once GSC-0044 runs by itself (requests.log ENT-272), waits. No ship of ours lost. The repair asks about 180 steel plate and 45 circuit boards (30% of the catalog's build materials, the game's help), carried from this turn by supply-repair-gsc-0044-plate and -boards.
Cause: the tool system still printed both facilities `active` (the faction reading in data/empire/empire.json, last written 2026-11-18 01:04 UTC, 91 hours before; empire.py collect has not run since the resume), and no check reads a facility's state from the game at a turn's start. An outpost in lawless space stood three days with no ship of ours signed in.
Fix, done: the turn skill logistics-stock now opens with step 0, a free faction_owned read: any facility not ready is the turn's first work. Asked: the empire reading running again and the reserve gate (requests.log ENT-294); how an outpost is kept while the fleet is away, before Atria (ENT-295); what wrecked it (ENT-296, Oracle).
Proposed, @Unity: empire.py collect raises an alert (fleet view=alerts, the briefing) when a facility of ours reads damaged or a base wrecked, so it fires without a member's read.
Would it have prevented this one: the wreck, no; the three days unseen, yes for my turns from now; the alert would show it to every member at once.

